  at the end of the day that's just how  comics work bad guys are shown to be  ridiculously powerful to make it seem  like the heroes have no chance of  defeating them because they're way  overpowered but at the end of the day  the heroes find a way to win because  they're the good guys but even then a  demonic entity who conquered an entire  dimension filled with millions of worlds  lost to teenagers but with that out of  the way we can get into trigon's powers  which are so immense that they basically  encompass everything and what i mean by  that is since trigon is the  personification of evil he's made of  evil energy and therefore has vast  demonic powers that he can use in  practically any way he wishes not  surprisingly trigon has superhuman  strength speed and durability but that  barely scratches the surface of what  trigon is capable of i mean barely  scratches the surface right this guy  also possesses omniscience meaning that  he knows everything that can be known as  well as precognition meaning that he  also knows what will occur before it  happens he's also a powerful telekinetic  and when i say powerful i don't mean  that he can just move some really heavy  stuff with his mind i mean that he can  literally use his telekinesis to alter  space and time as well as manipulate  matter trigen is also a powerful magic  wielder and can warp reality with only a  thought he can destroy matter on a  subatomic level which defies the laws of  physics and was able to turn every  person on earth to stone which requires  a great proficiency in matter  manipulation not only is he able to  destroy and transform matter but he's  also able to create something from  nothing which is even more evidence that  the natural laws of the universe simply  don't apply to him trigon can also  teleport interdimensionally and is even  able to break down dimensional barriers  he can also channel his mystic energy  into beams called a death stare that's  powerful enough to destroy planets and  during a battle with the teen titans  dragon brags about destroying galaxies  and universes which would place him well  beyond omega level and furthermore the  monitor states that dragon's power level  is in the same ballpark as the spectres  which would make him one of the most  powerful entities in the dc universe and  the most powerful entity in the dc  universe to basically lose to teenagers  now like nearly every character in dc  dragon's origin was altered by the new  52 reboot this version of trigon was  born eons ago in a different universe  where three entities known as the divine  were trying to rid their universe of  evil to accomplish this they used the  heart of darkness a planet-sized object  that siphoned evil out of everything it  touches and when they discover that a  world they'd already purged of evil had  once again been consumed with evil they  return and one of them reveals himself  to basically be trigon who absorbs the  heart of darkness which contains all of  the evil from the universes it had also  drained and so this version of trigan is  pretty much the embodiment of evil just  like the pre-flashpoint version was and  so after absorbing the heart of darkness  trigen sets out across multiple  universes looking for more evil to  devour and dragon conquers multiple  worlds turning each of them into hellish  versions of themselves and his plan is  to basically leave a son behind on each  to rule in his place however only three  of these sons survive and he doesn't  view any of them as a worthy successor  eventually one of his minions brings him  a woman from earth and they have a  daughter who of course would be raven of  the teen titans and after seeing how  powerful she is he decides that earth  women are suitable mothers for the army  of children that he wants in order to  help him rule the universe and much like  the pre-flash point version of trigon  the new 52 version is extremely powerful  even before absorbing the heart of  